<p>(e) Sodium metal can be used to distinguish between cyclopentanone and 1-methylcyclopentanol. 1-methylcyclopentanol reacts with Na, forming sodium 1-methylcyclopentanolate and releasing H2 bubbles. Cyclopentanone does not react with sodium metal. </p>

